{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/init()"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/init()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"init","roleHeading":"Initializer","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:6Yorkie0A19_V1_TreeRestoreSpanVACycfc","title":"init()","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Inherited from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Message.init()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"references":{"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie":{"role":"collection","title":"Yorkie","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeRestoreSpan carries a tree node run from a single deletion, addressed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by TreeNodeID identity, for identity-preserving Tree undo\/redo. Unlike the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text RestoreSpan (flat offsets), a tree span records the node’s structure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(type\/attrs) and its position anchors, because in a tree id-order is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sibling-order: left_sibling_id and right_sibling_id are redundant external"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary anchors of the deleted run, so restore can reconstruct the run’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal order from the op’s own spans and needs only one surviving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary to place it. value\/attributes are a deep copy so a GC-purged node"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be recreated."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan","title":"Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan"},"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan/init()":{"title":"init()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_TreeRestoreSpan\/init()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_treerestorespan\/init()","abstract":[]}}}